{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":489273,"ns":0,"title":"Artinian ring","extract":"In mathematics, specifically abstract algebra, an Artinian ring (sometimes Artin ring) is a ring that satisfies the descending chain condition on (one-sided) ideals; that is, there is no infinite descending sequence of ideals. Artinian rings are named after Emil Artin, who first discovered that the descending chain condition for ideals simultaneously generalizes finite rings and rings that are finite-dimensional vector spaces over fields.","description":"Ring in abstract algebra","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}